  "files": [
    {
      "path": "TEMPLATE.md",
      "name": "TEMPLATE.md",
      "kind": "source",
      "source": "# Web64-C Stack ABI Starter\n\nA freestanding C90 project using the recursive Web64 Stack ABI v1.\n\n## Architecture Notes: Why this architecture?\n\nC owns gameplay state while the SDK supplies typed hardware access and dependency-linked helpers.\n\nThe project uses Build Targets so artifact policy stays out of source code. Native assets remain editable and generated C/assembly bindings describe the same bytes. Optional runtime modules are target scoped and dead-strip when they are not selected.\n\n### Change these decisions when\n\n- profiling identifies a measured hot path or memory collision;\n- the target hardware, video standard, or artifact type changes;\n- a project-specific renderer has outgrown the generic extension hook.\n\n### Keep these decisions when\n\n- the change only hides C64 hardware behavior behind another abstraction;\n- it would duplicate bytes already owned by a native Web64 asset;\n- it would move frame-critical work from a bounded assembly path into an unmeasured loop.\n\n## First Modification\n\nAdd state to update() and keep hardware writes in render().\n\n\n## Project Contract\n\n- Entry: main.c\n- Language: C\n- Compiler ABI: web64-stack-v1\n- Video: PAL\n- Native assets: none\n- Compatibility modules: none\n\n\n## References\n\n- semantic-inspiration: [Commodore 64 Programmer Reference Guide](https://archive.org/details/c64-programmer-ref)\n\nThis file belongs to the generated project. Updating the bundled template never mutates this project.\n"
    },
